---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import ProofPoint from '../components/ProofPoint.astro';
import CTAButton from '../components/CTAButton.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Google Distributed Cloud"
  description="C-9INE helps banks, government institutions and critical-infrastructure organisations turn Google Distributed Cloud into a secure, production-ready operating platform."
>
  <!--
    This page follows the C-9INE GDC Executive Booklet (v1.0) page for
    page, in order: Problem, Belief, How It Works, What We Standardise,
    Customer Outcomes, then the booklet's own closing page. Proof is the
    one section added beyond the booklet itself. Plain stacked sections
    throughout — no pinned/sliding scroll mechanic.
  -->
  <PageIntro eyebrow="Google Distributed Cloud">
    <h1>One platform. Less chaos.</h1>
    <p class="gdc-subhead">Run VMs and containers on your infrastructure with a cloud operating model.</p>
    <p class="lede">
      Your infrastructure. Cloud operating model. Sovereign control. C-9INE helps banks,
      government and critical-infrastructure organisations turn Google Distributed Cloud into a
      secure, production-ready operating platform — covering everything from readiness to
      capability transfer.
    </p>
    <div class="page-intro__cta">
      <CTAButton href="/contact?intent=gdc-pilot">Book a GDC pilot scoping call</CTAButton>
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="booklet-panel">
        <span class="section-number">01</span>
        <p class="eyebrow">The Problem</p>
        <h2>Your data centre was not meant to become this complicated.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          VMware, Nutanix, Hyper-V, Kubernetes and cloud projects often grow into separate
          platforms, each with its own skills and operating model.
        </p>

        <ol class="numbered-rows">
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">01</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Licensing pressure</h4>
              <p>Renewals, bundles and platform overlap make budgeting harder.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">02</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Platform sprawl</h4>
              <p>Different stacks create different tools, teams and runbooks.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">03</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Skills fragmentation</h4>
              <p>Specialists are spread across too many operating models.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">04</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Operational overhead</h4>
              <p>Security, compliance and lifecycle controls are repeated in each stack.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="statement">
          More platforms did not create simplicity. They created another operating problem.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="booklet-panel">
        <span class="section-number">02</span>
        <p class="eyebrow">The Belief</p>
        <h2>Modernisation should reduce complexity, not move it somewhere else.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          Google Distributed Cloud brings a cloud operating model to infrastructure you
          control, so VMs and containers can move in one strategic direction.
        </p>

        <div class="plus-row">
          <span class="plus-row__item">VMs</span>
          <span class="plus-row__sign">+</span>
          <span class="plus-row__item">Containers</span>
          <span class="plus-row__sign">+</span>
          <span class="plus-row__item">Policy</span>
          <span class="plus-row__sign">+</span>
          <span class="plus-row__item">Operations</span>
        </div>

        <p class="statement">One platform for legacy workloads and modern applications.</p>

        <p class="lede">
          The platform experience matters because customers need a controlled path from today's
          estate to tomorrow's cloud model.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="booklet-panel">
        <span class="section-number">03</span>
        <p class="eyebrow">How It Works</p>
        <h2>From fragmented estates to a single operating model.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          A practical path that translates today's infrastructure into repeatable GDC
          architecture, governance and operations.
        </p>

        <ol class="numbered-rows">
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">01</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Assess</h4>
              <p>Inventory platforms, renewal timing, dependencies and workload fit.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">02</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Consolidate</h4>
              <p>Converge VMs and containers closer to one platform direction.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">03</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Govern</h4>
              <p>Apply consistent policy, security, IAM and lifecycle controls.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">04</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Operate</h4>
              <p>Standardise observability, automation and handover practices.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="statement">
          Assess the estate. Consolidate the platform. Govern consistently. Operate with
          confidence.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="booklet-panel">
        <span class="section-number">04</span>
        <p class="eyebrow">What We Standardise</p>
        <h2>The foundations every GDC programme depends on.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          C-9INE helps industrialise the patterns that are too important to rebuild manually,
          platform by platform.
        </p>

        <ul class="domains-grid">
          <li>
            <svg class="domains-grid__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="12" rx="1.5" />
              <path d="M12,16 L12,20" />
              <path d="M9,20 L15,20" />
            </svg>
            <div>
              <p class="domains-grid__label">VM runtime</p>
              <p class="domains-grid__desc">Run existing virtual machines under a cloud operating model</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg class="domains-grid__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <rect x="4" y="4" width="12" height="12" rx="2" />
              <rect x="8" y="8" width="12" height="12" rx="2" />
            </svg>
            <div>
              <p class="domains-grid__label">Kubernetes</p>
              <p class="domains-grid__desc">Standardise container platform operations</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg class="domains-grid__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <circle cx="12" cy="5" r="2" />
              <circle cx="5" cy="18" r="2" />
              <circle cx="19" cy="18" r="2" />
              <path d="M12,7 L6.5,16.3" />
              <path d="M12,7 L17.5,16.3" />
            </svg>
            <div>
              <p class="domains-grid__label">Networking</p>
              <p class="domains-grid__desc">Repeatable connectivity and segmentation patterns</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg class="domains-grid__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M12,3 L20,6 L20,12 C20,17 16.5,20.5 12,22 C7.5,20.5 4,17 4,12 L4,6 Z" />
              <path d="M8.5,12 L11,14.5 L16,9" />
            </svg>
            <div>
              <p class="domains-grid__label">IAM &amp; access</p>
              <p class="domains-grid__desc">Clear roles, permissions and boundaries</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg class="domains-grid__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M2,12 C5,6 19,6 22,12 C19,18 5,18 2,12 Z" />
              <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="2.5" />
            </svg>
            <div>
              <p class="domains-grid__label">Observability</p>
              <p class="domains-grid__desc">Logging, monitoring and operational visibility</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <svg class="domains-grid__icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
              <path d="M6,3 L15,3 L19,7 L19,21 L6,21 Z" />
              <path d="M15,3 L15,7 L19,7" />
              <path d="M9,12 L16,12 M9,15.5 L16,15.5 M9,9 L12,9" />
            </svg>
            <div>
              <p class="domains-grid__label">Security &amp; compliance</p>
              <p class="domains-grid__desc">Consistent guardrails and control evidence</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="statement">Standardisation is what turns infrastructure into a platform.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="booklet-panel">
        <span class="section-number">05</span>
        <p class="eyebrow">Customer Outcomes</p>
        <h2>From infrastructure estate to cloud operating model.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          The goal is not another technology island. The goal is a simpler, governed way to
          run today's workloads while modernising.
        </p>

        <ol class="numbered-rows">
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">01</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Reduce licensing pressure</h4>
              <p>Fewer duplicated platform layers.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">02</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Lower operational overhead</h4>
              <p>One model for VMs and containers.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">03</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Improve skills leverage</h4>
              <p>Common patterns across teams.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">04</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Strengthen control</h4>
              <p>Policy, security and visibility built in.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span class="numbered-rows__num mono-tag">05</span>
            <div>
              <h4>Modernise safely</h4>
              <p>Run today's workloads while building tomorrow's apps.</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <p class="statement">One platform. Less chaos.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof">
        <ProofPoint eyebrow="Proof">
          Live Saudi GDC delivery, not theoretical: a national regulator, a tier-one commercial
          bank, and a large-scale production rollout.
        </ProofPoint>
        <p class="lede proof__context">
          Delivered in the region's strictest regulatory environment, alongside Google Cloud's
          own Dammam region (me-central2) and the Class C licence CST granted it there.
        </p>

        <div class="proof__grid">
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Regulatory baseline</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              GDC software-only validated against sovereign data, operational compliance and
              security expectations, for a national financial regulator.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Tier-one commercial bank</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Mission-critical legacy applications and microservices coexisting on
              customer-owned infrastructure, in production.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Large-scale production rollout</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Anthos-to-GDC migration path and multi-cluster architecture readiness, delivered
              at scale.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">VM Runtime, in production</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Live at a Saudi bank today — VMs and containers governed under one operating
              model, not a lab environment.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="proof__card">
            <p class="proof__card-tag mono-tag">Sovereign AI, natively</p>
            <p class="proof__card-desc">
              Gemini runs inside the platform, including fully air-gapped, so model inference
              never has to leave the building.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="proof__assets">
          <span class="proof__assets-label mono-tag">Reusable assets</span>
          <div class="proof__tags">
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">HLD/LLD baselines</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">VM Runtime validation</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">Multi-DC bare-metal design</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">Migration factory runbooks</span>
            <span class="proof__tag mono-tag">Operational handover model</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight section-raised">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="closing">
        <h2>Your infrastructure. Cloud operating model. Sovereign control.</h2>
        <p class="lede">
          C-9INE helps organisations assess, design and deliver Google Distributed Cloud as a
          practical path from fragmented infrastructure to a more consistent operating model.
        </p>

        <ul class="closing__list">
          <li>VM and container consolidation</li>
          <li>Cloud-consistent operations</li>
          <li>Repeatable deployment and governance</li>
          <li>Part of the wider C-9INE cloud engineering approach</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="closing__cta">
          <CTAButton href="/contact?intent=gdc-pilot">Book a GDC pilot scoping call</CTAButton>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .gdc-subhead {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  /* Every booklet-page section shares this shape: a static page
     number, a blue eyebrow matching the booklet's own section labels,
     heading, intro copy, then whatever body content that page has. No
     scroll-hijacking or pinning anywhere on this page — every section
     just sits in normal document flow like the rest of the site. */
  .booklet-panel {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .section-number {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.5rem);
    /* A mix against transparent (not a flat gunmetal shade) so this
       ghost numeral stays faintly visible on both the plain and the
       .section-raised background alike, rather than matching one of
       them exactly and disappearing. */
    color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--white-smoke) 10%, transparent);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .booklet-panel h2 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--step-2);
  }

  .booklet-panel > .lede {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .numbered-rows {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--gunmetal-line);
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    overflow: hidden;
  }

  .numbered-rows li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 0.95rem 1.15rem;
    background: var(--gunmetal-raised);
  }

  .numbered-rows__num {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: var(--gunmetal);
    color: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  .numbered-rows h4 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .numbered-rows p {
    margin-top: 0.3rem;
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  /* The Belief section's "VMs + Containers + Policy + Operations"
     row, matching the booklet's own plus-separated block layout. */
  .plus-row {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.6rem;
  }

  .plus-row__item {
    padding: 0.6rem 1.1rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 30%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 8%, transparent);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .plus-row__sign {
    color: var(--aquamarine);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  /* What We Standardise's six-item foundation grid: icon, label,
     one-line description, two columns on wider screens. */
  .domains-grid {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 1.1rem 1.75rem;
  }

  .domains-grid li {
    display: flex;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    align-items: flex-start;
  }

  .domains-grid__icon {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 1.5rem;
    height: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 0.1rem;
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--aquamarine);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .domains-grid__label {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
  }

  .domains-grid__desc {
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .domains-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  /* The bold highlight box each booklet page closes on ("More
     platforms did not create simplicity...", "One platform. Less
     chaos.", etc.). */
  .statement {
    margin-top: 1.75rem;
    padding: 1rem 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 35%, transparent);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--aquamarine) 8%, transparent);
    color: var(--white-smoke);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
  }

  .proof__context {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    max-width: 46rem;
  }

  .proof__grid {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
  }

  .proof__card {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    border-radius: var(--border-radius);
    background: var(--gunmetal-raised);
  }

  .proof__card-tag {
    color: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  .proof__card-desc {
    margin-top: 0.6rem;
    color: var(--silver);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .proof__assets {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.75rem 0.6rem;
  }

  .proof__assets-label {
    color: var(--silver);
  }

  .proof__tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
  }

  .proof__tag {
    padding: 0.35rem 0.75rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--gunmetal-line);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--silver) 6%, transparent);
    color: var(--silver);
  }

  .closing {
    max-width: 40rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .closing h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }

  .closing .lede {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .closing__list {
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 2.75rem);
    display: inline-flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.65rem;
    text-align: left;
    color: var(--silver);
  }

  .closing__list li {
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .closing__list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.5em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--aquamarine);
  }

  .closing__cta {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }
</style>
